=== HINT 1 ===
Struct definition syntax:
  struct Point {
      double x;
      double y;
  };

=== HINT 2 ===
Access members with dot notation: a.x, a.y, b.x, b.y
sqrt() is in <math.h> - link with -lm if needed.

=== HINT 3 ===
Compile note: if you get a linker error about sqrt, add -lm flag.
CFarer passes -lm automatically on Linux/macOS via the build command.
On Windows with MSVC or MinGW, math is linked by default.

=== HINT 4 (SPOILER) ===
struct Point { double x; double y; };

double distance(struct Point a, struct Point b) {
    double dx = b.x - a.x;
    double dy = b.y - a.y;
    return sqrt(dx*dx + dy*dy);
}
